<div class="ssn">Halachah 1 (LM I:36): Krias Shma, the Twelve Tribes, and Seventy Facets</div>

<div class="p">Every Jewish soul is rooted in the seventy souls of Yaakov's house → rooted in the seventy facets of Torah (shiv'in anpin nehirin = seventy luminous facets). Opposite them: seventy nations = seventy dark facets (shiv'in anpin chashuchin). The desire for licentiousness is the generality of all evil traits of the seventy nations. Tikun: saying Shma and Baruch Shaim (12 words = 12 tribes; 49 letters = 49 letters of the tribes' names). Through accepting Malchus Shamayim, one's soul is included in the twelve tribes (= the G-d-fearing woman, the mistress). The desire (= the harlot, the evil maidservant) then flees: "I am fleeing from my mistress Sarai." Closing eyes during Shma = subduing the "beautiful maiden who has no eyes" (= the desire). Torah's light is simple — imaged according to the vessel. Guarding the Bris perfects the vessel → light imaged as blessing. The Bedtime Shma applies all this to sleep: "may my bed be complete" = included in the twelve tribes. "Enlighten my eyes" = seventy luminous facets (vs. seventy dark facets = death). A talmid chacham constantly attached to Torah is exempt. Viduy before sleep separates the soul from the seventy nations. "Vihi No'am" = pleasantness of Torah. "Sixty mighty men" = 600,000 who received Torah, each imaging their letter. "His sword upon his thigh" = guarding the Bris = making mnemonic signs = holy vessels.</div>

<div class="ssn">Halachah 2 (LM I:35): Sleep, Emunah, Chashmal, and the Renewal of the Mind</div>

<div class="p">Guard the intellect from external wisdoms and foreign thoughts. The mind must be renewed constantly — through sleep ("new each morning, great is Your faithfulness"). During sleep, the mind/soul enters emunah. But emunah itself must be guarded from the chitzonim drawing sustenance — one draws Chashmal from the world of Binah to clothe and protect the emunah. How to draw Chashmal: (1) conducting business with perfect faithfulness (like Rav Safra — "speaks truth in his heart"); (2) reciting Krias Shma with mesirus nefesh (= soul included in Binah/Ima Ila'ah → Chashmal drawn from there). Viduy before sleep = emes = truth in the heart → draws Chashmal from Binah (= Yom Kippur). When Chashmal guards the emunah, sleep is a great good: the mind is renewed. This is the tikun for the flaw of thought/emission: the exhausted mind needs sleep to be renewed; but sleep without the protection of Chashmal is dangerous. Krias Shma She'al HaMitah with kavvanah and mesirus nefesh = the complete tikun. "Behold, You desire truth in the inner parts — and in the hidden, You make wisdom known to me" = viduy (truth) → in the hidden (sleep/s'simu d'mochin) → new wisdom (renewed mind). "Into Your hand I entrust my spirit" = delivering the soul into emunah (= hands = "his hands were emunah"). "You have redeemed me, Hashem, G-d of truth" = emes draws Chashmal for protection. "HaShkivainu — spread over us the shelter of Your peace" = Chashmal = Ima d'masachchas al b'naha (Mother sheltering children). Chashmal = gematria of b'shalom.</div>

